IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `cbca-core`
IMPORT `cbca-core-definitions`
IMPORT `cb4-common`
IMPORT `cb4-amendment`

-- Canada Business Corporations Act (R.S.C. 1985, c. C-44), Part XV, ss 181 to 186.1: AMALGAMATION.
--
-- UNOFFICIAL. Encoded from a plain-text rendering of the Department of Justice Canada consolidation
-- current to 2026-09-30; not verified against the official text.
--
-- WHAT THIS MODULE IS. How two or more corporations join into one ("amalgamate"): who may (s 181), what
-- the agreement must contain (s 182), how the shareholders approve it, class by class (s 183), the two
-- short forms that dispense with the agreement and the meeting (s 184), the articles, the creditors'
-- declaration and notice, and the certificate (s 185), what the certificate does (s 186), and
-- amalgamations made under other federal Acts (s 186.1).
--
-- Dates are asked as DATEs; the Act fixes none in this range. The 30 days a creditor has to object are
-- counted with the keel's convention (fork F1 in the keel): the date of the notice is day 0, and day 30 is
-- in time.

§§ `s 181 Amalgamation`

-- src:2194 | Amalgamation
-- src:2195 | 181 Two or more corporations, including holding and subsidiary corporations, may amalgamate and continue as one corporation.
@ref CBCA s 181 (src:2195)
GIVEN `the number of corporations that propose to amalgamate` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the corporations may amalgamate and continue as one corporation within s 181` MEANS
    `the number of corporations that propose to amalgamate` AT LEAST 2

§§ `s 182 Amalgamation agreement`

-- The agreement, as the facts the paragraphs ask of it. (d) applies only if some shares are not to be
-- converted into securities of the amalgamated corporation; (f) asks whether the by-laws are those of one
-- of the amalgamating corporations and, if they are not, for a copy of the proposed by-laws.
-- src:2196 | Amalgamation agreement
-- src:2197 | 182 (1) Each corporation proposing to amalgamate shall enter into an agreement setting out the terms and means of effecting the amalgamation and, in particular, setting out
-- src:2198 | (a) the provisions that are required to be included in articles of incorporation under section 6;
-- src:2199 | (b) the name and address of each proposed director of the amalgamated corporation;
-- src:2200 | (c) the manner in which the shares of each amalgamating corporation are to be converted into shares or other securities of the amalgamated corporation;
-- src:2201 | (d) if any shares of an amalgamating corporation are not to be converted into securities of the amalgamated corporation, the amount of money or securities of any body corporate that the holders of such shares are to receive in addition to or instead of securities of the amalgamated corporation;
-- src:2202 | (e) the manner of payment of money instead of the issue of fractional shares of the amalgamated corporation or of any other body corporate the securities of which are to be received in the amalgamation;
-- src:2203 | (f) whether the by-laws of the amalgamated corporation are to be those of one of the amalgamating corporations and, if not, a copy of the proposed by-laws; and
-- src:2204 | (g) details of any arrangements necessary to perfect the amalgamation and to provide for the subsequent management and operation of the amalgamated corporation.
@ref CBCA s 182(1) (src:2197-2204)
DECLARE `Amalgamation agreement (s 182)` HAS
    `every corporation proposing to amalgamate has entered into the agreement` IS A BOOLEAN
    `sets out the provisions required to be in articles of incorporation under section 6` IS A BOOLEAN
    `sets out the name and address of each proposed director of the amalgamated corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
    `sets out how the shares of each amalgamating corporation are to be converted into shares or other securities of the amalgamated corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
    `some shares of an amalgamating corporation are not to be converted into securities of the amalgamated corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
    `sets out the money or securities those holders are to receive in addition to or instead of securities of the amalgamated corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
    `sets out how money is to be paid instead of fractional shares` IS A BOOLEAN
    `states whether the by-laws are to be those of one of the amalgamating corporations` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the by-laws are not to be those of one of the amalgamating corporations` IS A BOOLEAN
    `includes a copy of the proposed by-laws` IS A BOOLEAN
    `sets out details of arrangements necessary to perfect the amalgamation and provide for the subsequent management and operation` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref CBCA s 182(1) (src:2197-2204)
GIVEN agreement IS A `Amalgamation agreement (s 182)`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the amalgamation agreement contains what s 182(1) requires` MEANS
        agreement's `every corporation proposing to amalgamate has entered into the agreement`
    AND agreement's `sets out the provisions required to be in articles of incorporation under section 6`
    AND agreement's `sets out the name and address of each proposed director of the amalgamated corporation`
    AND agreement's `sets out how the shares of each amalgamating corporation are to be converted into shares or other securities of the amalgamated corporation`
    AND (    (NOT agreement's `some shares of an amalgamating corporation are not to be converted into securities of the amalgamated corporation`)
         OR  agreement's `sets out the money or securities those holders are to receive in addition to or instead of securities of the amalgamated corporation`)
    AND agreement's `sets out how money is to be paid instead of fractional shares`
    AND agreement's `states whether the by-laws are to be those of one of the amalgamating corporations`
    AND (    (NOT agreement's `the by-laws are not to be those of one of the amalgamating corporations`)
         OR  agreement's `includes a copy of the proposed by-laws`)
    AND agreement's `sets out details of arrangements necessary to perfect the amalgamation and provide for the subsequent management and operation`

-- "Cancellation": shares of one amalgamating corporation held by or on behalf of another amalgamating
-- corporation are cancelled without repayment of capital and are not converted.
-- src:2205 | Cancellation
-- src:2206 | (2) If shares of one of the amalgamating corporations are held by or on behalf of another of the amalgamating corporations, the amalgamation agreement shall provide for the cancellation of such shares when the amalgamation becomes effective without any repayment of capital in respect thereof, and no provision shall be made in the agreement for the conversion of such shares into shares of the amalgamated corporation.
@ref CBCA s 182(2) (src:2206)
GIVEN `shares of one amalgamating corporation are held by or on behalf of another of them` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the agreement provides for their cancellation without any repayment of capital` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the agreement makes provision for their conversion into shares of the amalgamated corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the agreement deals as s 182(2) requires with shares held within the group` MEANS
        (NOT `shares of one amalgamating corporation are held by or on behalf of another of them`)
    OR  (    `the agreement provides for their cancellation without any repayment of capital`
         AND (NOT `the agreement makes provision for their conversion into shares of the amalgamated corporation`))

§§ `s 183 Shareholder approval`

-- The directors' duty to put the agreement to a meeting of the shareholders arises for an amalgamation
-- under s 182 and not for a short-form amalgamation under s 184 (which dispenses with s 183).
-- src:2207 | Shareholder approval
-- src:2208 | 183 (1) The directors of each amalgamating corporation shall submit the amalgamation agreement for approval to a meeting of the holders of shares of the amalgamating corporation of which they are directors and, subject to subsection (4), to the holders of each class or series of such shares.
@ref CBCA s 183(1) (src:2208)
GIVEN `the amalgamation is proposed under the agreement of section 182 and not as a short-form amalgamation under section 184` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the directors of each amalgamating corporation must submit the agreement to a meeting of shareholders within s 183(1)` MEANS
    `the amalgamation is proposed under the agreement of section 182 and not as a short-form amalgamation under section 184`

-- The notice: complying with s 135 (piece cb3, a plain input), sent to each shareholder of each
-- amalgamating corporation, with a copy or summary of the agreement, and stating the right to dissent.
-- src:2209 | Notice of meeting
-- src:2210 | (2) A notice of a meeting of shareholders complying with section 135 shall be sent in accordance with that section to each shareholder of each amalgamating corporation, and shall
-- src:2211 | (a) include or be accompanied by a copy or summary of the amalgamation agreement; and
-- src:2212 | (b) state that a dissenting shareholder is entitled to be paid the fair value of their shares in accordance with section 190, but failure to make that statement does not invalidate an amalgamation.
@ref CBCA s 183(2) (src:2210-2212)
GIVEN -- out of range: section 135 (piece cb3)
      `the notice complies with section 135` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice is sent to each shareholder of each amalgamating corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice includes or is accompanied by a copy or summary of the amalgamation agreement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a dissenting shareholder is entitled to be paid the fair value of their shares in accordance with section 190` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice states that a dissenting shareholder is entitled to be paid the fair value of their shares` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the notice of the meeting complies within s 183(2)` MEANS
        `the notice complies with section 135`
    AND `the notice is sent to each shareholder of each amalgamating corporation`
    AND `the notice includes or is accompanied by a copy or summary of the amalgamation agreement`
    AND (    (NOT `a dissenting shareholder is entitled to be paid the fair value of their shares in accordance with section 190`)
         OR  `the notice states that a dissenting shareholder is entitled to be paid the fair value of their shares`)

@ref CBCA s 183(2)(b) (src:2212)
GIVEN `the omission of the dissent statement was the only failure of the notice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Effect on validity of leaving out the dissent statement`
`the effect on the amalgamation of leaving out the dissent statement within s 183(2)(b)` MEANS
    `the effect of leaving out the dissent statement` `the omission of the dissent statement was the only failure of the notice`

-- "Each share carries the right to vote ... whether or not it otherwise carries the right to vote": the
-- answer is yes whatever the share's ordinary voting right is (tested).
-- src:2213 | Right to vote
-- src:2214 | (3) Each share of an amalgamating corporation carries the right to vote in respect of an amalgamation agreement whether or not it otherwise carries the right to vote.
@ref CBCA s 183(3) (src:2214)
GIVEN `the share otherwise carries the right to vote` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the share carries the right to vote on the amalgamation agreement within s 183(3)` MEANS TRUE

-- "Would entitle such holders to vote as a class or series under section 176": the agreement's provision
-- is asked as if it were in a proposed amendment to the articles, using the amendment module's rule.
-- src:2215 | Class vote
-- src:2216 | (4) The holders of shares of a class or series of shares of each amalgamating corporation are entitled to vote separately as a class or series in respect of an amalgamation agreement if the amalgamation agreement contains a provision that, if contained in a proposed amendment to the articles, would entitle such holders to vote as a class or series under section 176.
@ref CBCA s 183(4) (src:2216)
GIVEN effect IS A `Effect of a proposed amendment on a class of shares (s 176(1))`
      `the articles provide that the holders may not vote separately` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the new class would be constrained under paragraph 174(1)(c) and is otherwise equal to the class` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amendment only adds a right to convert into an otherwise equal class constrained under paragraph 174(1)(c)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the holders hold a series of shares of a class` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the series is affected in a manner different from other shares of the same class` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the holders of a class or series are entitled to vote separately on the amalgamation agreement within s 183(4)` MEANS
    `the holders of a class or series are entitled to vote separately within s 176(1) and s 176(4)` effect `the articles provide that the holders may not vote separately` `the new class would be constrained under paragraph 174(1)(c) and is otherwise equal to the class` `the amendment only adds a right to convert into an otherwise equal class constrained under paragraph 174(1)(c)` `the holders hold a series of shares of a class` `the series is affected in a manner different from other shares of the same class`

-- The shareholders of ONE amalgamating corporation have approved when their special resolution has passed
-- and, subject to subsection (4), each class or series entitled to vote separately has approved by a
-- special resolution (fork F1: in addition, as for s 176(6)).
-- src:2217 | Shareholder approval
-- src:2218 | (5) Subject to subsection (4), an amalgamation agreement is adopted when the shareholders of each amalgamating corporation have approved of the amalgamation by special resolutions.
@ref CBCA s 183(5) (src:2218)
GIVEN tally IS A `Vote tally`
      `every class or series entitled to vote separately has approved by special resolution` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the shareholders of an amalgamating corporation have approved the agreement within s 183(5)` MEANS
        `special resolution within s 2(1)` tally
    AND `every class or series entitled to vote separately has approved by special resolution`

-- The agreement is adopted when the shareholders of EACH amalgamating corporation have approved: one
-- answer per corporation, from the rule above.
@ref CBCA s 183(5) (src:2218)
GIVEN `the approval of each amalgamating corporation's shareholders` IS A LIST OF BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the amalgamation agreement is adopted within s 183(5)` MEANS
    all (GIVEN approved YIELD approved) `the approval of each amalgamating corporation's shareholders`

-- "Notwithstanding approval of the agreement by the shareholders of all or any of the amalgamating
-- corporations": the directors of an amalgamating corporation may terminate it if the agreement says so
-- and no certificate of amalgamation has yet been issued.
-- src:2219 | Termination
-- src:2220 | (6) An amalgamation agreement may provide that at any time before the issue of a certificate of amalgamation the agreement may be terminated by the directors of an amalgamating corporation, notwithstanding approval of the agreement by the shareholders of all or any of the amalgamating corporations.
@ref CBCA s 183(6) (src:2220)
GIVEN `the agreement provides that the directors may terminate it before a certificate of amalgamation is issued` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a certificate of amalgamation has been issued` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the directors may terminate the agreement notwithstanding the shareholders' approval within s 183(6)` MEANS
        `the agreement provides that the directors may terminate it before a certificate of amalgamation is issued`
    AND (NOT `a certificate of amalgamation has been issued`)

§§ `s 184 Short-form amalgamation`

-- "Vertical": a holding corporation with one or more of its subsidiaries. All the issued shares of each
-- amalgamating subsidiary are held by one or more of the other amalgamating corporations (paragraph a.1),
-- and the directors' resolutions provide for cancellation, the same articles as the holding corporation
-- (except as prescribed) and no new securities. "Except as may be prescribed" is a plain input: whether
-- the articles differ only in a prescribed way.
-- src:2221 | Vertical short-form amalgamation
-- src:2222 | 184 (1) A holding corporation and one or more of its subsidiary corporations may amalgamate and continue as one corporation without complying with sections 182 and 183 if
-- src:2223 | (a) the amalgamation is approved by a resolution of the directors of each amalgamating corporation;
-- src:2224 | (a.1) all of the issued shares of each amalgamating subsidiary corporation are held by one or more of the other amalgamating corporations; and
-- src:2225 | (b) the resolutions provide that
-- src:2226 | (i) the shares of each amalgamating subsidiary corporation shall be cancelled without any repayment of capital in respect thereof,
-- src:2227 | (ii) except as may be prescribed, the articles of amalgamation shall be the same as the articles of the amalgamating holding corporation, and
-- src:2228 | (iii) no securities shall be issued by the amalgamated corporation in connection with the amalgamation and the stated capital of the amalgamated corporation shall be the same as the stated capital of the amalgamating holding corporation.
@ref CBCA s 184(1) (src:2222-2228)
GIVEN `the corporations are a holding corporation and one or more of its subsidiary corporations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the directors of each amalgamating corporation approved the amalgamation by resolution` IS A BOOLEAN
      `all the issued shares of each amalgamating subsidiary corporation are held by one or more of the other amalgamating corporations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the resolutions provide that the shares of each amalgamating subsidiary corporation are cancelled without any repayment of capital` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the resolutions provide that the articles of amalgamation are the same as the holding corporation's, except as may be prescribed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the resolutions provide that no securities are issued and the stated capital is the same as the holding corporation's` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the corporations may amalgamate without complying with sections 182 and 183 within s 184(1)` MEANS
        `the corporations are a holding corporation and one or more of its subsidiary corporations`
    AND `the directors of each amalgamating corporation approved the amalgamation by resolution`
    AND `all the issued shares of each amalgamating subsidiary corporation are held by one or more of the other amalgamating corporations`
    AND `the resolutions provide that the shares of each amalgamating subsidiary corporation are cancelled without any repayment of capital`
    AND `the resolutions provide that the articles of amalgamation are the same as the holding corporation's, except as may be prescribed`
    AND `the resolutions provide that no securities are issued and the stated capital is the same as the holding corporation's`

-- "Horizontal": two or more wholly-owned subsidiaries of the same holding body corporate.
-- src:2229 | Horizontal short-form amalgamation
-- src:2230 | (2) Two or more wholly-owned subsidiary corporations of the same holding body corporate may amalgamate and continue as one corporation without complying with sections 182 and 183 if
-- src:2231 | (a) the amalgamation is approved by a resolution of the directors of each amalgamating corporation; and
-- src:2232 | (b) the resolutions provide that
-- src:2233 | (i) the shares of all but one of the amalgamating subsidiary corporations shall be cancelled without any repayment of capital in respect thereof,
-- src:2234 | (ii) except as may be prescribed, the articles of amalgamation shall be the same as the articles of the amalgamating subsidiary corporation whose shares are not cancelled, and
-- src:2235 | (iii) the stated capital of the amalgamating subsidiary corporations whose shares are cancelled shall be added to the stated capital of the amalgamating subsidiary corporation whose shares are not cancelled.
@ref CBCA s 184(2) (src:2230-2235)
GIVEN `the corporations are two or more wholly-owned subsidiary corporations of the same holding body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the directors of each amalgamating corporation approved the amalgamation by resolution` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the resolutions provide that the shares of all but one of the amalgamating subsidiary corporations are cancelled without any repayment of capital` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the resolutions provide that the articles of amalgamation are the same as those of the subsidiary whose shares are not cancelled, except as may be prescribed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the resolutions provide that the stated capital of the subsidiaries whose shares are cancelled is added to that of the subsidiary whose shares are not cancelled` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the subsidiary corporations may amalgamate without complying with sections 182 and 183 within s 184(2)` MEANS
        `the corporations are two or more wholly-owned subsidiary corporations of the same holding body corporate`
    AND `the directors of each amalgamating corporation approved the amalgamation by resolution`
    AND `the resolutions provide that the shares of all but one of the amalgamating subsidiary corporations are cancelled without any repayment of capital`
    AND `the resolutions provide that the articles of amalgamation are the same as those of the subsidiary whose shares are not cancelled, except as may be prescribed`
    AND `the resolutions provide that the stated capital of the subsidiaries whose shares are cancelled is added to that of the subsidiary whose shares are not cancelled`

§§ `s 185 Sending of articles, declarations, notice to creditors, certificate`

-- The duty to send arises once the amalgamation has been adopted under s 183 or approved under s 184 and
-- the agreement was not terminated under s 183(6) (the "subject to subsection 183(6)").
-- src:2236 | Sending of articles
-- src:2237 | 185 (1) Subject to subsection 183(6), after an amalgamation has been adopted under section 183 or approved under section 184, articles of amalgamation in the form that the Director fixes shall be sent to the Director together with the documents required by sections 19 and 106.
@ref CBCA s 185(1) (src:2237)
GIVEN `the amalgamation has been adopted under section 183` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amalgamation has been approved under section 184` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the directors terminated the agreement under subsection 183(6)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the corporation must send articles of amalgamation to the Director within s 185(1)` MEANS
        (    `the amalgamation has been adopted under section 183`
         OR  `the amalgamation has been approved under section 184`)
    AND (NOT `the directors terminated the agreement under subsection 183(6)`)

-- The articles go "together with the documents required by sections 19 and 106" (pieces cb1 and cb2).
@ref CBCA s 185(1) (src:2237)
GIVEN `the articles of amalgamation are in the form that the Director fixes` IS A BOOLEAN
      -- out of range: sections 19 and 106 (pieces cb1 and cb2)
      `the documents required by sections 19 and 106 are sent with them` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the articles of amalgamation have been sent as s 185(1) requires` MEANS
        `the articles of amalgamation are in the form that the Director fixes`
    AND `the documents required by sections 19 and 106 are sent with them`

-- "To the satisfaction of the Director" is a judgment the Act hands to the Director: it is an input, not
-- a guess. The grounds are a director's or officer's statutory declaration, attached to the articles, for
-- EACH amalgamating corporation.
-- src:2238 | Attached declarations
-- src:2239 | (2) The articles of amalgamation shall have attached thereto a statutory declaration of a director or an officer of each amalgamating corporation that establishes to the satisfaction of the Director that
-- src:2240 | (a) there are reasonable grounds for believing that
-- src:2241 | (i) each amalgamating corporation is and the amalgamated corporation will be able to pay its liabilities as they become due, and
-- src:2242 | (ii) the realizable value of the amalgamated corporation’s assets will not be less than the aggregate of its liabilities and stated capital of all classes; and
-- src:2243 | (b) there are reasonable grounds for believing that
-- src:2244 | (i) no creditor will be prejudiced by the amalgamation, or
-- src:2245 | (ii) adequate notice has been given to all known creditors of the amalgamating corporations and no creditor objects to the amalgamation otherwise than on grounds that are frivolous or vexatious.
@ref CBCA s 185(2) (src:2239-2245)
GIVEN `a statutory declaration of a director or an officer of each amalgamating corporation is attached to the articles` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there are reasonable grounds for believing that each amalgamating corporation is and the amalgamated corporation will be able to pay its liabilities as they become due` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there are reasonable grounds for believing that the realizable value of the amalgamated corporation's assets will not be less than the aggregate of its liabilities and stated capital of all classes` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there are reasonable grounds for believing that no creditor will be prejudiced by the amalgamation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there are reasonable grounds for believing that adequate notice has been given to all known creditors of the amalgamating corporations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there are reasonable grounds for believing that no creditor objects otherwise than on grounds that are frivolous or vexatious` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Director is satisfied that the declaration establishes those grounds` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the statutory declaration meets s 185(2)` MEANS
        `a statutory declaration of a director or an officer of each amalgamating corporation is attached to the articles`
    AND `there are reasonable grounds for believing that each amalgamating corporation is and the amalgamated corporation will be able to pay its liabilities as they become due`
    AND `there are reasonable grounds for believing that the realizable value of the amalgamated corporation's assets will not be less than the aggregate of its liabilities and stated capital of all classes`
    AND (    `there are reasonable grounds for believing that no creditor will be prejudiced by the amalgamation`
         OR  (    `there are reasonable grounds for believing that adequate notice has been given to all known creditors of the amalgamating corporations`
              AND `there are reasonable grounds for believing that no creditor objects otherwise than on grounds that are frivolous or vexatious`))
    AND `the Director is satisfied that the declaration establishes those grounds`

-- "Adequate notice" (subsection (3)): (a) a written notice to each known creditor whose claim exceeds one
-- thousand dollars; (b) one publication in a newspaper at the registered office's place plus reasonable
-- notice in each province where the corporation carries on business; (c) each notice states the intention
-- to amalgamate with specified corporations and that a creditor may object within thirty days of the
-- notice's date. A claim of exactly 1,000 dollars does not "exceed" one thousand dollars.
-- src:2246 | Adequate notice
-- src:2247 | (3) For the purposes of subsection (2), adequate notice is given if
-- src:2248 | (a) a notice in writing is sent to each known creditor having a claim against the corporation that exceeds one thousand dollars;
-- src:2249 | (b) a notice is published once in a newspaper published or distributed in the place where the corporation has its registered office and reasonable notice thereof is given in each province where the corporation carries on business; and
-- src:2250 | (c) each notice states that the corporation intends to amalgamate with one or more specified corporations in accordance with this Act and that a creditor of the corporation may object to the amalgamation within thirty days from the date of the notice.
@ref CBCA s 185(3)(a) (src:2248)
GIVEN `the creditor's claim against the corporation in dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the creditor must be sent a written notice within s 185(3)(a)` MEANS
    `the creditor's claim against the corporation in dollars` GREATER THAN 1000

@ref CBCA s 185(3) (src:2247-2250)
GIVEN `a written notice was sent to each known creditor having a claim that exceeds one thousand dollars` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a notice was published once in a newspaper published or distributed in the place of the registered office` IS A BOOLEAN
      `reasonable notice of it was given in each province where the corporation carries on business` IS A BOOLEAN
      `each notice states that the corporation intends to amalgamate with one or more specified corporations in accordance with this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `each notice states that a creditor may object within thirty days from the date of the notice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`adequate notice has been given to creditors within s 185(3)` MEANS
        `a written notice was sent to each known creditor having a claim that exceeds one thousand dollars`
    AND `a notice was published once in a newspaper published or distributed in the place of the registered office`
    AND `reasonable notice of it was given in each province where the corporation carries on business`
    AND `each notice states that the corporation intends to amalgamate with one or more specified corporations in accordance with this Act`
    AND `each notice states that a creditor may object within thirty days from the date of the notice`

-- The last day a creditor may object: thirty days from the date of the notice (that day included).
@ref CBCA s 185(3)(c) (src:2250)
GIVEN `the date of the notice` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day on which a creditor may object within s 185(3)(c)` MEANS
    `the last day of` (`Time limit` WITH `number of units` IS 30, `unit of time` IS `calendar days`) `counted from` `the date of the notice`

-- src:2251 | Certificate of amalgamation
-- src:2252 | (4) On receipt of articles of amalgamation, the Director shall issue a certificate of amalgamation in accordance with section 262.
@ref CBCA s 185(4) (src:2252)
GIVEN `the Director has received articles of amalgamation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the Director must issue a certificate of amalgamation within s 185(4)` MEANS
    `the Director has received articles of amalgamation`

§§ `s 186 Effect of certificate`

-- Each paragraph takes effect "on the date shown in a certificate of amalgamation": from that date on, the
-- paragraph's effect holds. One shared helper asks whether the day is on or after the date shown.
-- src:2253 | Effect of certificate
-- src:2254 | 186 On the date shown in a certificate of amalgamation
@ref CBCA s 186, helper (src:2254)
GIVEN `the date shown in the certificate of amalgamation` IS A DATE
      `the day asked about` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the day is on or after the date shown in the certificate of amalgamation` MEANS
    `the day asked about` AT LEAST `the date shown in the certificate of amalgamation`

-- src:2255 | (a) the amalgamation of the amalgamating corporations and their continuance as one corporation become effective;
@ref CBCA s 186(a) (src:2255)
GIVEN `the date shown in the certificate of amalgamation` IS A DATE
      `the day asked about` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the amalgamation and continuance as one corporation are effective on a day within s 186(a)` MEANS
    `the day is on or after the date shown in the certificate of amalgamation` `the date shown in the certificate of amalgamation` `the day asked about`

-- src:2256 | (b) the property of each amalgamating corporation continues to be the property of the amalgamated corporation;
@ref CBCA s 186(b) (src:2256)
GIVEN `the date shown in the certificate of amalgamation` IS A DATE
      `the day asked about` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the property of each amalgamating corporation is the amalgamated corporation's on a day within s 186(b)` MEANS
    `the day is on or after the date shown in the certificate of amalgamation` `the date shown in the certificate of amalgamation` `the day asked about`

-- src:2257 | (c) the amalgamated corporation continues to be liable for the obligations of each amalgamating corporation;
@ref CBCA s 186(c) (src:2257)
GIVEN `the date shown in the certificate of amalgamation` IS A DATE
      `the day asked about` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the amalgamated corporation is liable for the obligations of each amalgamating corporation on a day within s 186(c)` MEANS
    `the day is on or after the date shown in the certificate of amalgamation` `the date shown in the certificate of amalgamation` `the day asked about`

-- src:2258 | (d) an existing cause of action, claim or liability to prosecution is unaffected;
@ref CBCA s 186(d) (src:2258)
GIVEN `the date shown in the certificate of amalgamation` IS A DATE
      `the day asked about` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`an existing cause of action, claim or liability to prosecution is unaffected on a day within s 186(d)` MEANS
    `the day is on or after the date shown in the certificate of amalgamation` `the date shown in the certificate of amalgamation` `the day asked about`

-- src:2259 | (e) a civil, criminal or administrative action or proceeding pending by or against an amalgamating corporation may be continued to be prosecuted by or against the amalgamated corporation;
@ref CBCA s 186(e) (src:2259)
GIVEN `the date shown in the certificate of amalgamation` IS A DATE
      `the day asked about` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a pending proceeding by or against an amalgamating corporation may be continued by or against the amalgamated corporation on a day within s 186(e)` MEANS
    `the day is on or after the date shown in the certificate of amalgamation` `the date shown in the certificate of amalgamation` `the day asked about`

-- src:2260 | (f) a conviction against, or ruling, order or judgment in favour of or against, an amalgamating corporation may be enforced by or against the amalgamated corporation; and
@ref CBCA s 186(f) (src:2260)
GIVEN `the date shown in the certificate of amalgamation` IS A DATE
      `the day asked about` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a conviction, ruling, order or judgment may be enforced by or against the amalgamated corporation on a day within s 186(f)` MEANS
    `the day is on or after the date shown in the certificate of amalgamation` `the date shown in the certificate of amalgamation` `the day asked about`

-- src:2261 | (g) the articles of amalgamation are deemed to be the articles of incorporation of the amalgamated corporation and the certificate of amalgamation is deemed to be the certificate of incorporation of the amalgamated corporation.
@ref CBCA s 186(g) (src:2261)
GIVEN `the date shown in the certificate of amalgamation` IS A DATE
      `the day asked about` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the articles and the certificate of amalgamation are deemed the articles and certificate of incorporation on a day within s 186(g)` MEANS
    `the day is on or after the date shown in the certificate of amalgamation` `the date shown in the certificate of amalgamation` `the day asked about`

§§ `s 186.1 Amalgamation under other federal Acts`

-- The other Acts: the Bank Act, the Canada Cooperatives Act, the Cooperative Credit Associations Act, the
-- Insurance Companies Act and the Trust and Loan Companies Act. When the amalgamation is not under one of
-- them, this subsection does not speak: NOTHING.
-- src:2262 | Amalgamation under other federal Acts
-- src:2263 | 186.1 (1) Subject to subsection (2), a corporation may not amalgamate with one or more bodies corporate pursuant to the Bank Act, the Canada Cooperatives Act, the Cooperative Credit Associations Act, the Insurance Companies Act or the Trust and Loan Companies Act unless the corporation is first authorized to do so by the shareholders in accordance with section 183.
@ref CBCA s 186.1(1) (src:2263)
GIVEN `the amalgamation is with bodies corporate pursuant to one of the listed federal Acts` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the shareholders first authorized it in accordance with section 183` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the corporation may amalgamate pursuant to another federal Act within s 186.1(1)` MEANS
    IF `the amalgamation is with bodies corporate pursuant to one of the listed federal Acts`
    THEN JUST `the shareholders first authorized it in accordance with section 183`
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:2264 | Short-form amalgamations
-- src:2265 | (2) A corporation may not amalgamate with one or more bodies corporate pursuant to the provisions of one of the Acts referred to in subsection (1) respecting short-form amalgamations unless the corporation is first authorized to do so by the directors in accordance with section 184.
@ref CBCA s 186.1(2) (src:2265)
GIVEN `the amalgamation is a short-form amalgamation pursuant to one of the listed federal Acts` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the directors first authorized it in accordance with section 184` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the corporation may amalgamate in short form pursuant to another federal Act within s 186.1(2)` MEANS
    IF `the amalgamation is a short-form amalgamation pursuant to one of the listed federal Acts`
    THEN JUST `the directors first authorized it in accordance with section 184`
    ELSE NOTHING

-- The Director's duty on receipt of a notice "satisfactory to the Director": the satisfaction is a fact.
-- src:2266 | Discontinuance
-- src:2267 | (3) On receipt of a notice satisfactory to the Director that a corporation has amalgamated pursuant to one of the Acts referred to in subsection (1), the Director shall file the notice and issue a certificate of discontinuance in accordance with section 262.
@ref CBCA s 186.1(3) (src:2267)
GIVEN `the Director has received a notice that the corporation has amalgamated pursuant to one of the listed federal Acts` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice is satisfactory to the Director` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the Director must file the notice and issue a certificate of discontinuance within s 186.1(3)` MEANS
        `the Director has received a notice that the corporation has amalgamated pursuant to one of the listed federal Acts`
    AND `the notice is satisfactory to the Director`

-- A deeming provision: the notice counts as articles in the form the Director fixes, for section 262.
-- src:2268 | Notice deemed to be articles
-- src:2269 | (4) For the purposes of section 262, a notice referred to in subsection (3) is deemed to be articles that are in the form that the Director fixes.
@ref CBCA s 186.1(4) (src:2269)
GIVEN `the document is a notice referred to in subsection 186.1(3)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the notice is deemed to be articles in the form the Director fixes for section 262 within s 186.1(4)` MEANS
    `the document is a notice referred to in subsection 186.1(3)`

-- "Ceases to apply ... on the date shown": the Act applies before that date and not on or after it
-- (fork F2).
-- src:2270 | Act ceases to apply
-- src:2271 | (5) This Act ceases to apply to the corporation on the date shown in the certificate of discontinuance.
@ref CBCA s 186.1(5) (src:2271)
GIVEN `the date shown in the certificate of discontinuance` IS A DATE
      `the day asked about` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`this Act still applies to the corporation on a day within s 186.1(5)` MEANS
    `the day asked about` LESS THAN `the date shown in the certificate of discontinuance`

-- src:2272 | Non-application
-- src:2273 | (6) For greater certainty, section 185 does not apply to a corporation that amalgamates pursuant to one of the Acts referred to in subsection (1).
@ref CBCA s 186.1(6) (src:2273)
GIVEN `the corporation amalgamates pursuant to one of the listed federal Acts` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 185 does not apply to the corporation within s 186.1(6)` MEANS
    `the corporation amalgamates pursuant to one of the listed federal Acts`
